 ## Feature switches
 
-| Variable               | Default         | Effect                                                                                                                                                  |
-| ---------------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
-| `TICKET_BOARD_ENABLED` | `false`         | Turns the ticket board on for every account. Otherwise each person turns it on in **Settings → Labs**. Set it on the API and worker.                    |
-| `USER_DEVICES_ENABLED` | on              | `false` stops signed-in desktop apps from letting bots run commands on the user's own computer. Set it on the API and worker.                           |
-| `PI_SESSION_RECORDING` | off             | `true` records agent sessions as JSONL under `DATA_DIR/pi-sessions`. The files are not encrypted, so do not use it on a shared or multi-tenant install. |
-| `PRIVACY_POLICY_URL`   | Rakazo's policy | The privacy policy linked from the AI data-sharing notice. Set it on the API.                                                                           |
+| Variable                             | Default         | Effect                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |
+| ------------------------------------ | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `TICKET_BOARD_ENABLED`               | `false`         | Turns the ticket board on for every account. Otherwise each person turns it on in **Settings → Labs**. Set it on the API and worker.                                                                                                        |
+| `USER_DEVICES_ENABLED`               | on              | `false` stops signed-in desktop apps from letting bots run commands on the user's own computer. Set it on the API and worker.                                                                                                              |
+| `PI_SESSION_RECORDING`               | off             | `true` records agent sessions as JSONL under `DATA_DIR/pi-sessions`. The files are not encrypted, so do not use it on a shared or multi-tenant install.                                                                                    |
+| `PRIVACY_POLICY_URL`                 | Rakazo's policy | The privacy policy linked from the AI data-sharing notice. Set it on the API.                                                                                                                                                              |
+| `RAKAZO_FAST_REPLY`                  | on              | `0` turns off the early line a bot says on the fast tier while a slow model is still starting its real turn. See [Reply speed](#reply-speed). Set it on the worker.                                                                        |
+| `RAKAZO_FAST_REPLY_MODEL`            | the run's model | A model id on the same connection that answers the early line faster. Unset asks the run's own model, with thinking off and a short output cap.                                                                                            |
+| `RAKAZO_FAST_REPLY_TIMEOUT_MS`       | `6000`          | How long the early line may take before it is dropped. 500–30000.                                                                                                                                                                          |
+| `RAKAZO_MID_TURN_PROGRESS_MIN_AGE_MS` | `60000`        | How long a turn must have run before a bot may post a durable mid-turn message. Lower it, for example `5000`, when people write while the bot works and expect an answer then.                                                              |
+| `RAKAZO_MID_TURN_PROGRESS_MAX_PER_RUN` | `3`            | How many durable mid-turn messages one run may post.                                                                                                                                                                                       |
+
+## Reply speed
+
+A reasoning model can spend several seconds before it shows a word. Two settings make a bot feel
+present in that gap, and both belong on the worker:
+
+- **Fast tier.** While the real turn starts, the worker asks the same model connection for one
+  short line — a warm "on it", or the greeting of a bot that was just created — with thinking off
+  and a 96-token cap, and streams it into the chat. It is dropped the moment the real turn says
+  anything, so a fast model pays nothing for it. Name a smaller model on the same connection with
+  `RAKAZO_FAST_REPLY_MODEL` to make the line arrive sooner still, and turn the whole thing off with
+  `RAKAZO_FAST_REPLY=0`.
+- **Mid-turn messages.** A bot that answers a message sent while it works posts it as a mid-turn
+  chat message, which waits until a turn has run for `RAKAZO_MID_TURN_PROGRESS_MIN_AGE_MS`. Lower
+  that, and raise `RAKAZO_MID_TURN_PROGRESS_MAX_PER_RUN`, on a deployment whose people write
+  mid-task.
 
